OL,4,CFewer frosts, more hot days in UK    W5
OL,5,                                      W5
OL,6,GThe UK's seasons are changing, with  W5
OL,7,Gfewer winter frosts and more hot     W5
OL,8,Gsummer days, according to new        W5
OL,9,Ganalysis from the Met Office.        W5
OL,10,                                      W5
OL,11,GAcross the UK, the number of winter  W5
OL,12,Gdays with an air frost ` when the    W5
OL,13,Gair temperature falls to 0C or below W5
OL,14,G` was around a quarter lower in the  W5
OL,15,Gdecade to 2025 than during the       W5
OL,16,Gperiod from 1961 to 1990.            W5
OL,17,                                      W5
OL,18,GIn southern England, the reduction   W5
OL,19,Gwas around a third while the average W5
OL,20,Gnumber of UK summer days reaching    W5
OL,21,G25C has more than doubled.           W5
OL,22,                                      W5
